{"context":"ADR-029 introduced human ownership into EKA: the `mbr` token, the `assigned-to` relationship, member-scoped projections and the assign/reassign/unassign commands. In practice EKA is used by a single author; ownership adds a token, a relationship, a conditional R13 sub-check, a projection surface, MCP workspace ops and skill-pack role mapping for a team model that is not exercised - while attribution (`author`/`by`/`by-kind`) already records provenance.","decision":"Remove work-ownership from EKA via deprecate-in-place, NOT hard-delete. Remove the authoring and surface: `eka assign/reassign/unassign`, the MCP workspace assignment tools, ownership prose in the skill pack, and the skill-pack role mapping (RoleVocabulary, ModeDelegate, mappings/*.toml, DELEGATION.txt). Keep `mbr` and `assigned-to` recognized on read for one major so frozen `exchange/snapshots`, `shr` sharing objects and this repo's self-hosting `AGENTS.md` keep loading. Provide the one-shot `eka migrate v2` to unlink `assigned-to` edges and retire `mbr` lines forward-only. Attribution/provenance (`author`/`by`/`by-kind`, incl. `worker`) STAYS - it is provenance, not assignment.","consequences":"EKA becomes a solo-author knowledge system with a smaller surface. Readers keep working through the deprecation window; hard-removal is a later major. ADR-029's team model is superseded for future work while its artifacts remain readable. Migration is explicit and forward-only. Cost: reader tolerance must be maintained and tested for one major.","alternativesConsidered":"Hard-delete `mbr`/`assigned-to` immediately (rejected: breaks frozen snapshots, shr sharing objects and the self-hosting AGENTS.md). Keep ownership and document it as optional (rejected: retains surface with no exercised value). Move ownership into a separate product (rejected: no consumer, would add a store writer).","appliesTo":["eka-standard/**","eka-core/**","eka-cli/**","eka-mcp/**"]}